WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
I had applied about a month ago to Sedgwick, and they had rejected me at the time.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.440
They reached out to me, I think, yesterday, and another one reached out too.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.920
I'm supposed to be going to Texas next week with Pilot.

4
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.760
They were onboarding me as a staff adjuster.

5
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.560
I don't think I would have been able to do it, you know, or it would have taken me four

6
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.520
times as long trying to find the information on the internet.

7
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.280
I would, I would definitely refer them.

8
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.880
I would send them right your way because you gotta have that foundation.

9
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.160
Gotta have that step by step. And then what's really cool about it is, if you need to take

10
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.560
a break, take a break. If you need to pause, pause.

11
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.320
And that self-paced, I think, is really good.

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:47.480
If I had sat in on, let's say, just a marathon workshop, 15 hours, by the end of even three

13
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.480
hours, I'm lost.

14
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.040
You don't get time to absorb it.

15
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.920
But I would totally send somebody your way for that reason, that you could self-pace.

16
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.920
You do it.

17
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:56.920
You can do it after hours.

18
00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:57.920
You can do it,

19
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.160
you know, if you have a day off. I see it as an investment more than a cost.

20
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.920
If I had to do a CAT tomorrow, I could.
